# Belt and braces: production configuration comes from Vercel, never from a file on a laptop.
#
# ⚠ Next.js loads .env.local at RUNTIME with HIGHER precedence than platform environment
# variables. So if a local env file ever reaches a deployment bundle, the live app runs on
# whatever that file says -- and this one defines APP_DATABASE_URL (the DEV app_runtime
# connection) and NEXTAUTH_SECRET. A production deployment pointed at the dev database is a
# silent, total failure of every DB-backed route.
#
# The Vercel CLI is understood to exclude .env* by default. This states it explicitly rather
# than relying on that, because the cost of being wrong is the whole site and the default is
# not something this repo controls.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Never ship local notes, scratch work or the scanner's token into a deployment.
.farmflow-scanner
scratchpad
